# Inc-R1 RED proofs + verification transcript — Lane R, batch 2026-10-10-perf-batch

Worker: Kimi (kimi-code/kimi-for-coding) via the kimi CLI. All commands run from
the worktree root; all paths relative. Product change under test: span clipping
in `mapper/canvas.py` (`Canvas.elbow_down`, `Canvas.edge`). Bytecode cache off
(`python -B`, `-p no:cacheprovider`).

## 0 · The product change (GREEN state)

`mapper/canvas.py`: both span loops now clip to the canvas rectangle BEFORE
iterating (`edge`: `range(max(0, min(y0,y1)), min(h-1, max(y0,y1)) + 1)`;
`elbow_down`: vertical drop `range(max(0, y0+1), min(ybus, h))` under a
`0 <= ybus < h` guard, bus row `range(max(0, xa+1), min(xb, w))`). Every skipped
cell is one `wire` would have dropped (`canvas.py:107-109`), so painted cells
stay byte-identical.

sha256 of the shipped `mapper/canvas.py` (before any mutation, and restored to
after every mutation):

    d354bd46424a0a8d2f459b6d56903eb0df96baff8164a9e74e5b92e3d14838a2 *mapper/canvas.py

