## 2 · MEASURED wire count and geometry (AT-075, recorded per LLR-PERF.1.1)

- Session: wide-2000 (`build_wide(2000)`, one root + 1999 children), terminal
  geometry 118x34 (`run_test(size=(118, 34))`), real keys `l` then `j` through
  `MapperApp(tmp_path)`; counting wrapper on `Canvas.wire`; counter RESET after
  mount so mount paints are not charged.
- Measured: **12,264 `Canvas.wire` calls** for the two keypresses.
- Cap asserted: `<= 1,200,000` (requirement; tightened from 4,800,000 so a
  Y-only clip fails).
- Baseline for the same session pre-change: 23,983,998 calls (PERF0C SS7.1) —
  the shipped clip is ~1/1957 of the baseline. Round-2 probe p4 at wide-2000,
  one render: no clip 524,313 · x-only 6,547 · y-only 524,313 · x+y 6,547 —
  the measured 12,264 ≈ 2 x 6,132 matches the x-clipped order exactly.

## 3 · RED proof 1 — M-R1b (non-equivalent: clamp bus upper bound to min(xb, w-1))

Mutation: `mapper/canvas.py` bus loop `min(xb, self.w)` -> `min(xb, self.w - 1)`
(drops the in-bounds tail cell (w-1, ybus) whenever xb >= w). Copy of the
shipped file kept at `.dev-flow/2026-10-10-perf-batch/evidence/r1-canvas-clipped.py`.

    $ sha256sum mapper/canvas.py   # BEFORE
    d354bd46424a0a8d2f459b6d56903eb0df96baff8164a9e74e5b92e3d14838a2 *mapper/canvas.py

    $ python -B -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider tests/test_perf_paint_clip.py::test_bare_canvas_clip_equality
    FAILED tests/test_perf_paint_clip.py::test_bare_canvas_clip_equality[case1]
    1 failed, 8 passed in 0.38s        # case1 = bus span reaching past the right edge

    $ cp .dev-flow/2026-10-10-perf-batch/evidence/r1-canvas-clipped.py mapper/canvas.py
    $ sha256sum mapper/canvas.py   # AFTER restore — byte-identical
    d354bd46424a0a8d2f459b6d56903eb0df96baff8164a9e74e5b92e3d14838a2 *mapper/canvas.py

    $ python -B -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider tests/test_perf_paint_clip.py::test_bare_canvas_clip_equality
    9 passed in 0.36s

Verdict: KILLED by `test_bare_canvas_clip_equality` — the mutant drops one
in-bounds cell; the other 8 in-bounds shapes stay green (one mutation, one
conjunct). (The render-grid identity node would also catch it via the
right-edge-hugging goldens; the bare-canvas node is the named oracle.)

## 4 · RED proof 2 — Y-ONLY clip vs the cap

Mutation: `mapper/canvas.py` bus row x-loop unclipped —
`range(max(0, xa + 1), min(xb, self.w))` -> `range(xa + 1, xb)` (y loops still
clipped; painted bytes stay identical, so only the count can fail).

    $ python -B -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider tests/test_perf_paint_clip.py::test_at_075_keypress_wire_budget
    AT-075 wire calls (l,j, counter reset after mount): 23983998
    FAILED tests/test_perf_paint_clip.py::test_at_075_keypress_wire_budget - AssertionError...
    1 failed in 17.21s

    $ cp .dev-flow/2026-10-10-perf-batch/evidence/r1-canvas-clipped.py mapper/canvas.py
    $ sha256sum mapper/canvas.py   # AFTER restore — byte-identical
    d354bd46424a0a8d2f459b6d56903eb0df96baff8164a9e74e5b92e3d14838a2 *mapper/canvas.py

Verdict: KILLED by the wire cap — the x-axis carries the whole gain (23,983,998
calls, exactly the unclipped baseline). The golden-equality conjunct of the
same node stayed green under this mutant, as designed (painted bytes do not
change); the count conjunct reddens.

## 5 · RED proof 3 — M-R1a (remove the clip entirely)

Mutation: `mapper/canvas.py` restored to the HEAD (pre-change, unclipped) body.

    $ git show HEAD:mapper/canvas.py > mapper/canvas.py   # clip removed
    $ python -B -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider tests/test_perf_paint_clip.py::test_wire_count_budget
    wire calls for l,j on wide-2000 at 118x34 (counter reset after mount): 23983998 (baseline 23983998, cap 1200000)
    FAILED tests/test_perf_paint_clip.py::test_wire_count_budget - AssertionError...
    1 failed in 16.76s

    $ cp .dev-flow/2026-10-10-perf-batch/evidence/r1-canvas-clipped.py mapper/canvas.py
    $ rm .dev-flow/2026-10-10-perf-batch/evidence/r1-canvas-clipped.py
    $ sha256sum mapper/canvas.py   # AFTER restore — byte-identical to the shipped clip
    d354bd46424a0a8d2f459b6d56903eb0df96baff8164a9e74e5b92e3d14838a2 *mapper/canvas.py

Verdict: KILLED by the wire-count budget oracle (23,983,998 > 1,200,000).

